WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.099 --> 00:00:04.540
There’s recently been some pretty huge leaks
and rumors concerning Apple’s 2019 iPhones,

00:00:04.540 --> 00:00:08.440
so we thought we’d round them all up so
you guys can get a good idea of what to expect

00:00:08.440 --> 00:00:09.890
in September.

00:00:09.890 --> 00:00:13.240
Let’s get started!

00:00:13.240 --> 00:00:18.670
About a week ago, renders of a 2019 iPhone
11 with a triple-lens rear camera were leaked

00:00:18.670 --> 00:00:23.010
by OnLeaks, but the implementation of the
camera seemed far from what would be designed

00:00:23.010 --> 00:00:24.010
by Apple.

00:00:24.010 --> 00:00:28.500
The report from Digin.in didn’t give any
reason for the triple-lens camera, but earlier

00:00:28.500 --> 00:00:33.690
reports showed that Apple was interested in
Sony’s 3D camera time-of-flight technology,

00:00:33.690 --> 00:00:38.960
which is able to map rooms in real-time for
augmented reality and increase camera autofocus

00:00:38.960 --> 00:00:40.090
performance.

00:00:40.090 --> 00:00:43.809
That sounds exciting and it totally seems
like something Apple would do, but that rear

00:00:43.809 --> 00:00:45.519
camera design was awful.

00:00:45.519 --> 00:00:51.389
Thankfully, a couple of days ago, CompareRaja
released exclusively leaked renders of a horizontally

00:00:51.389 --> 00:00:53.069
stacked triple-lens camera.

00:00:53.069 --> 00:00:56.159
Now this one looks more like what Apple would
actually release.

00:00:56.159 --> 00:01:00.519
The interesting thing we see here is that
the flash is actually built into a ring around

00:01:00.519 --> 00:01:03.440
the center lens, and I’m loving this idea.

00:01:03.440 --> 00:01:07.890
Alternatively, Ben Geskin created renders
of the triple-lens rear camera in the same

00:01:07.890 --> 00:01:11.729
position as the current iPhone XS, and that
may actually make more sense.

00:01:11.729 --> 00:01:12.729
Looking at the renders, you’ll also notice
slightly thinner bezels on the display, so

00:01:12.729 --> 00:01:13.729
I’ve got no reason to complain.

00:01:13.729 --> 00:01:16.260
Just yesterday, more info was leaked about
the new iPhone 11.

00:01:16.260 --> 00:01:21.360
CompareRaja noted that two of the three rear
sensors are 10 and 14 megapixels.

00:01:21.360 --> 00:01:24.090
Details of the third sensor are still unknown.

00:01:24.090 --> 00:01:28.640
The selfie camera was also noted to pack a
10-megapixel sensor which I’m really excited

00:01:28.640 --> 00:01:31.390
about since there’s still a lot of room
to grow there.

00:01:31.390 --> 00:01:36.450
Recent rumors from DigiTimes and Jean-Baptise
Su claimed that the 2019 iPhone 11 would switch

00:01:36.450 --> 00:01:41.259
from a Lightning port to USB-C, but CompareRaja
seems to disagree.

00:01:41.259 --> 00:01:45.440
They noted that the 2019 iPhone will still
pack a Lightning port, but we won’t know

00:01:45.440 --> 00:01:46.960
for sure until September.

00:01:46.960 --> 00:01:51.820
Either way, we expect this year’s iPhone
to come with the new 18W USB-C charger in

00:01:51.820 --> 00:01:52.820
the box.

00:01:52.820 --> 00:01:57.090
Concerning Face ID, Ming-Chi Kuo is predicting
that Apple will increase the power output

00:01:57.090 --> 00:02:00.530
of the flood illuminator, which should make
Face ID more accurate.

00:02:00.530 --> 00:02:04.619
There’s also a chance that we’ll be seeing
the implementation of Vein ID, which would

00:02:04.619 --> 00:02:09.890
allow Face ID to scan the veins inside a users
face, making it even more secure, but we may

00:02:09.890 --> 00:02:12.750
not see that until at least 2020.

00:02:12.750 --> 00:02:17.020
Another thing we may not see this year is
5G data speeds, and I’m totally okay with

00:02:17.020 --> 00:02:18.020
that.

00:02:18.020 --> 00:02:22.550
4G LTE already supports download speeds much
faster than what even the iPhone XS is able

00:02:22.550 --> 00:02:26.000
to achieve, due to cellular provider limitations.

00:02:26.000 --> 00:02:31.090
As for the notch, Ben Geskin believes the
Infrared lens and front camera on 2019 iPhones

00:02:31.090 --> 00:02:35.400
will be integrated into each other, making
the notch smaller than it currently is.

00:02:35.400 --> 00:02:37.750
I, for one, wouldn’t mind this at all.

00:02:37.750 --> 00:02:40.660
But what about the complete removal of the
notch altogether?

00:02:40.660 --> 00:02:44.980
Now we most definitely shouldn’t expect
this until at least 2020, but there’s possibly

00:02:44.980 --> 00:02:48.210
a way for the TrueDepth camera array to work
from beneath the display.

00:02:48.210 --> 00:02:49.210
How?

00:02:49.210 --> 00:02:54.870
Well, AMS, an Austrian company, recently launched
an optical sensor that works from underneath

00:02:54.870 --> 00:02:56.370
an OLED display.

00:02:56.370 --> 00:03:00.450
This type of technology can be utilized by
Apple to implement the Face ID sensors under

00:03:00.450 --> 00:03:01.470
the display.

00:03:01.470 --> 00:03:06.070
As for the camera itself, it could be hidden
by using transparent OLED technology, which

00:03:06.070 --> 00:03:08.790
is already being used by TV manufacturers.

00:03:08.790 --> 00:03:12.590
The OLED pixels above the camera lens would
simply be turned off whenever you open the

00:03:12.590 --> 00:03:15.290
camera app or any other app that uses it.

00:03:15.290 --> 00:03:18.200
And when it’s not in used, you’ll get
a full-face display.

00:03:18.200 --> 00:03:20.720
Just don’t expect this for another couple
of years.

00:03:20.720 --> 00:03:26.170
A report from Barclays analyst Blaine Curtis
said that the 2019 iPhones could feature WiFi

00:03:26.170 --> 00:03:32.020
6, otherwise known as 802.11ax, which will
be anywhere from 4 to 10 times faster than

00:03:32.020 --> 00:03:34.700
the existing 802.11ac.

00:03:34.700 --> 00:03:38.540
To make it even better, it should increase
overall battery life due to a new feature

00:03:38.540 --> 00:03:40.490
called wake time scheduling.

00:03:40.490 --> 00:03:45.420
As for display technology, Apple could be
using Samsung’s Y-Octa OLED panel technology

00:03:45.420 --> 00:03:47.470
in the 2019 iPhones.

00:03:47.470 --> 00:03:51.870
This would integrate the touch-layer directly
into the OLED display, making it thinner and

00:03:51.870 --> 00:03:53.050
cheaper to produce.

00:03:53.050 --> 00:03:58.190
For this reason, we may see a complete switch
to OLED on all 2019 iPhone models, and as

00:03:58.190 --> 00:04:01.380
for Touch ID, don’t expect it come back
anymore.

00:04:01.380 --> 00:04:06.130
Ming-Chi Kuo says Face ID has become too accurate
and successful for us to need Touch ID anymore.

00:04:06.130 --> 00:04:10.980
He also said that we shouldn’t expect better
waterproofing any time soon since IP68 is

00:04:10.980 --> 00:04:14.130
already more than good enough for what most
users will need it for.

00:04:14.130 --> 00:04:16.440
And there’s one last thing before we end
this video..

00:04:16.440 --> 00:04:21.340
AirPower marketing material has been spotted
on a Malaysian site alongside the new iPhone

00:04:21.340 --> 00:04:22.910
Smart Battery case.

00:04:22.910 --> 00:04:27.120
This shows that Apple hasn’t abandoned AirPower,
and we’re likely to see a release sometime

00:04:27.120 --> 00:04:28.470
in 2019.

00:04:28.470 --> 00:04:32.600
So there you have it, there are all of the
2019 iPhone 11 leaks and rumors.

00:04:32.600 --> 00:04:35.940
Comment below if I missed any, and be sure
to subscribe so you don’t miss out on more

00:04:35.940 --> 00:04:36.900
videos like this one!

